Show the map's reading on the ruler; unify trigger color; fold the duplicate advisory

The ruler showed the rule but never the reading, so the highlighted band
read as "this is what was found" when it is actually "this is where the
closure line falls". Brian caught it as "where is the measurement?".

- The band the map actually read is now marked in accent teal and labeled
  "the map read this", set at verdict time alongside the map markers. The
  two are now visibly different bands: the closure line falls in "very
  low", the map read "low", one band to its right
- Deliberately a category and not a number: you cannot get a number off a
  color, and that gap IS the finding
- Trigger line, dot and label move from teal to warn amber so the line and
  the band it lands in read as one idea
- Band boxes: 46px -> 82px min height, .7rem -> .86rem type, real padding.
  They were compressing the text to unreadable at judging distance
- Map caption said "sample cluster" twice (my lead-in duplicated the
  positioning note from core/sites.py). Rewritten, and it now names the
  dark blue-gray wash as NOAA's own satellite layer so it does not read as
  a rendering fault or an edit of ours
- The advisory pane restated the verdict almost sentence for sentence.
  Folded into a closed <details> labeled as the report agent's own file,
  so the tool output stays as evidence without a wall of duplicate text

The source image is untouched. It is the frame the agent read, and editing
evidence to look nicer is the one thing this project does not do.

